    {
      "id": "q:u1-4-3:002",
      "lo": "lo:u1-4-3",
      "tier": "advanced",
      "type": "numeric",
      "stem": "Find the x-coordinate of the vertex of the curve of $f(x) = 2x^2 - 8x + 3$.",
      "answer": "2",
      "solution": [
        "For $f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c$, the vertex has x-coordinate $\\frac{-b}{2a}$.",
        "Here $a = 2$, $b = -8$: $x = \\frac{-(-8)}{2 \\times 2} = \\frac{8}{4} = 2$."
      ],
      "source_page": 22,
      "source_note": "Original question; general properties 1, p.22"
    },
    {
      "id": "q:u1-4-3:003",
      "lo": "lo:u1-4-3",
      "tier": "advanced",
      "type": "mcq",
      "stem": "The function $f(x) = -x^2 + 4x - 1$ has a…",
